1047
00:54:50.380 --> 00:54:55.380
Because now you've reestablished the water seal.

1048
00:54:55.380 --> 00:55:00.380
You understand it doesn't need clamps as long as it's underwater.

1049
00:55:00.380 --> 00:55:02.380
And it's better to be underwater than to be clamped.

1050
00:55:02.380 --> 00:55:06.380
Why is it better to be underwater, the end of the tube, underwater,

1051
00:55:06.380 --> 00:55:07.380
than for the tube to be clamped?

1052
00:55:07.380 --> 00:55:08.380
Why is it better?

1053
00:55:08.380 --> 00:55:09.380
Sterile.

1054
00:55:09.380 --> 00:55:12.380
No, not sterile necessary.

1055
00:55:12.380 --> 00:55:13.380
Necessarily.

1056
00:55:13.380 --> 00:55:19.380
Air can't go in, but stuff can come out.

1057
00:55:19.380 --> 00:55:21.380
If it's clamped, what's the problem?

1058
00:55:21.380 --> 00:55:24.380
Nothing can go in or out.

1059
00:55:24.380 --> 00:55:27.380
And you want stuff to come out.

1060
00:55:27.380 --> 00:55:29.380
You don't want stuff to go in.

1061
00:55:29.380 --> 00:55:33.380
So clamping is only a stop-gap measure.

1062
00:55:33.380 --> 00:55:35.380
It doesn't solve the problem.

1063
00:55:35.380 --> 00:55:37.380
What solves the problem?

1064
00:55:37.380 --> 00:55:39.380
Sticking the tube underwater.

1065
00:55:39.380 --> 00:55:40.380
So what is the order?

1066
00:55:40.380 --> 00:55:44.380
If they gave you a click and drag when the water seal breaks,

